Lane County, OR

************************************************************************


An invoice has been created for record request #26-825.

Greetings,



Lane County is in possession of some of records you have requested, as foll=
ows:



Regarding #3-7: Lane County does not possess any records.

Regarding #8: The records were readily available and will be produced short=
ly.



Regarding #1 and 2, we can perform an email search to see if Lane County ha=
s any records. See the spreadsheets: =E2=80=9C26-825_Public Records Request=
 Cost Estimate - Electronic Records.xlsx=E2=80=9D for details about the sea=
rch terms and cost. The charge for the records is $71.91, as calculated in =
the attached cost estimate.



We have reviewed and considered your request for a fee waiver and have deci=
ded to deny it.=20



There are two options for paying this estimate.



(1) Mail a check payable to Lane County Public Records to the following add=
ress:



Lane County Public Records

C/O County Counsel

125 E 8th Ave

Eugene, OR 97401



*You may also drop off the check at our office located at 125 E 8th Ave, Eu=
gene, OR 97401 during business hours. We are located on the 2nd floor of th=
e building. Please let us know if you choose this option so we can make sur=
e someone is available to meet you.



(2) Pay online via credit or debit card. If you choose to pay online, there=
 is a 2% convenience fee that is collected and received by the payment proc=
essor, Point &amp; Pay. Lane County Public Records does not receive this 2%=
 fee.



To pay your invoice online, click the link below. Enter the amount due: $71=
.91 and the invoice number: 26-825. You will receive a receipt for your tra=
nsaction via email from support@pointandpay.com.



Lane County Public Records Invoice Payment Portal



*Please note that the figures above are estimates. If the request takes mor=
e time than estimated, we will stop work on the request and wait to receive=
 additional payment before proceeding. If the request takes less time than =
estimated, we will send you a new estimate for the lower cost.



We will keep this request open for 60 days. If we do not receive payment wi=
thin 60 days, we will close this request and you will need to make a new on=
e. ORS 192.329(3)(b).



Sincerely,

Lane County Public Records








